WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:10.204
In August 2026, a catastrophic glacial flood tore through Langtang Valley, leaving over three hundred eighty tourists uncontactable and claiming thousands of lives.

2
00:00:10.154 --> 00:00:15.714
In steep Himalayan canyons, there is only one foot trail in, and one trail out.

3
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:20.952
Today's government warning systems rely solely on physical river sensors downstream.

4
00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:28.416
Sirens sound only after bridges are already washing away, giving people ten minutes to scale vertical cliffs in the pitch dark.

5
00:00:28.416 --> 00:00:36.952
This is HimalSanket: an AI-powered multi-hazard early warning and autonomous rescue system built so the next search doesn't take eleven days.

6
00:00:38.552 --> 00:00:41.621
HimalSanket doesn't guess or hallucinate.

7
00:00:41.571 --> 00:00:58.916
Our deterministic fusion engine combines five continuous vectors: catchment rainfall at thirty percent weight, Sentinel-2 glacial lake expansion at twenty-five percent, USGS seismic tremors at twenty percent, porter ground reports at fifteen percent, and geomorphic slope at ten percent.

8
00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:11.309
Using European Space Agency Sentinel-2 multispectral imagery, our pipeline monitors moraine lakes at five thousand meters altitude, tracking normalized difference water index expansion pixel by pixel.

9
00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:23.011
Simultaneously, Google's TimesFM foundation model forecasts precipitation spikes twenty-four hours in advance, allowing mountain communities to evacuate long before cloudbursts hit the ground.

10
00:01:24.611 --> 00:01:28.014
Watch what happens during an active emergency drill.

11
00:01:27.964 --> 00:01:38.523
When sensors detect an acute cloudburst surge, our FastAPI orchestrator on Google Cloud Run recalculates corridor risk in milliseconds, escalating from Moderate to Critical.

12
00:01:38.523 --> 00:01:50.904
Our GIS hydrodynamic model computes downstream wave arrival times: eighteen minutes to Lama Hotel gorge, thirty-eight minutes to Syabrubesi, and seventy-eight minutes to the Betrawati arterial bridge.

13
00:01:50.904 --> 00:02:04.869
Instantly, Google Gemini synthesizes telemetry into localized action directives in English, native Nepali, compressed SMS alerts for 2G phones, and one-click official SITREP reports for Nepal's Disaster Management Authority.

14
00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:10.490
Disaster tools fail if people on the ground cannot use them.

15
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:21.369
For local guides, porters, and trekkers, HimalSanket operates as an offline-first Progressive Web App. Porters walking through freezing monsoon rain cannot type text on a phone.

16
00:02:21.369 --> 00:02:26.178
With one tap, they record a ten-second voice note in their native dialect.

17
00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:37.107
Google Gemini transcribes the audio, extracting critical danger keywords like murky floodwaters, landslide cracks, or acoustic rumblings, directly boosting risk confidence.

18
00:02:37.107 --> 00:02:46.380
Trekkers can also consult our Gemini AI Safety Copilot for real-time trail guidance based on their live GPS elevation and distance to hazard zones.

19
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.776
When disaster strikes and a civilian is trapped, every kilobyte matters.

20
00:02:52.726 --> 00:03:02.821
HimalSanket's SOS Distress Capsule transmits ultralight micro-packets with exact GPS coordinates first, guaranteed to puncture fleeting 2G signal windows.

21
00:03:02.821 --> 00:03:11.035
At Search and Rescue headquarters, incoming distress calls are automatically prioritized by elevation vulnerability and medical urgency.

22
00:03:11.035 --> 00:03:22.083
With one click, commanders dispatch search and rescue helicopter sorties, streaming live telemetry, terrain clearance vectors, and real-time flight tracking directly to rescue teams.

23
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:29.335
Under the hood, Google Gemini provides multimodal reasoning and multilingual briefings.

24
00:03:29.285 --> 00:03:33.369
Google TimesFM delivers predictive rainfall forecasting.

25
00:03:33.369 --> 00:03:40.416
Cloud Run powers our microservice orchestrator, and Cloud Firestore synchronizes life-saving alerts in real time.

26
00:03:40.416 --> 00:03:44.416
Langtang has flooded and buried its people twice in a decade.

27
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:47.857
HimalSanket exists so there isn't a third time.

28
00:03:47.857 --> 00:03:49.238
Thank you.
